LOCUS       tL3                       88 bp    DNA              UNK 01-JAN-1980
DEFINITION  Bacteriophage lambda tL3, the rho-independent terminator of the
            major leftward (pL) operon just downstream of exo: 88 bp from the
            exo stop codon to the mapped termination point, carrying a GC-rich
            8-bp-stem / 5-nt-loop hairpin followed by the sequence of the
            CCUUUCU 3' end..
ACCESSION   tL3
VERSION     tL3
KEYWORDS    .
